const valleyGuide={name:'Valley',code:'c2',base:'https://www.rtjgolf.com/oxmoorvalley/tour-2013/',white:[393,153,363,152,334,334,475,358,472,393,288,490,147,502,340,146,337,366],par:[4,3,4,3,4,4,5,4,5,4,4,5,3,5,4,3,4,4],advice:["Downhill dogleg left plays shorter than its yardage. Longer hitters can carry left bunkers, but a drive too far right may run through the fairway.","Carry the pond to a green guarded by three front bunkers. Check the wind even if it feels calm at the tee.","Play to the 150-yard marker or left of it. Drives too far right create a difficult approach; a creek crosses the fairway short of 100 yards.","Take extra club. A short-left miss finds the pond; the middle or right side of the green is safer.","Dogleg right; avoid driving through the fairway left or trying to cut too much corner. Favor center-left of the green.","Favor the right side of the fairway and let the slope feed the ball to center. Control approach distance to the correct tier of the three-level green.","Watch the creek left. Long hitters may reach in two, but laying up short of the right fairway bunker is safer. The green is open in front.","Position the tee shot between the lake left and bunkers right. The green is deeper than it appears.","Aim for the 250-yard stake. Reaching in two is difficult; select the proper tier on the large, deep green.","Long dogleg right. Left is safer off the tee, while right shortens the approach. The deep green has three tiers.","Positioning matters more than length off the tee. Take extra club for the uphill approach and check the pin on the elevated green.","Aim for the 250-yard stake. Longer hitters may reach in two, but water right threatens and a front bunker guards the green.","Downhill par 3 plays a little shorter than the number. The Biarritz green can leave a difficult long putt.","Long hitters can shape a right-to-left drive over the left fairway bunker. If laying up, favor left; check the pin on the narrow three-tier green.","Find the center of the fairway between lake left and bunkers right. With a left pin, aim center and use the green slope.","Play to the center regardless of pin location. Sand and water guard the green; check the wind.","Slight dogleg right; favor right but avoid running through the fairway. Uphill approach to an elevated green plays longer.","Forced carry off the tee to find a level fairway lie. The approach is to an elevated multi-tier green; avoid missing left or long."]};
guideCourses.valley=[valleyGuide];
const ridgeGuide={name:'Ridge',code:'ridge',white:[364,500,506,356,123,389,317,129,363,361,373,440,137,333,353,165,396,543],par:[4,5,5,4,3,4,4,3,4,4,4,5,3,4,4,3,4,5],advice:["Take your tee shot down the middle on the slight dogleg-left opener. Carry the approach all the way to the green; shots short-left can roll back toward the fairway.","An accurate tee shot just left of center offers a chance to reach in two. Steep drop-offs beyond the right fairway bunker and along the left landing area make finding the fairway critical.","The signature par 5: position the drive right of the 250-yard stake, then lay up just past the 150-yard stake. The green against exposed shale rock is deeper than it looks.","Keep your tee shot well left of the right-side bunkers. Add a club for the uphill approach to the guarded green.","Avoid the bunker in front of the green. Aim for the center when the flag is near the edge.","Play to right-center fairway to avoid the deep ravine. The mid- to long-iron approach is to an elevated green with a pot bunker in front.","Favor left-center off the tee. Take an extra club for the uphill approach and avoid the bunkers right of the three-tier green.","Downhill par 3 plays one or two clubs shorter; wind matters. Avoid coming up short or going long.","Favor right-center off the tee. Take an extra club on the uphill approach and avoid the bunker left of the green.","On this dogleg-right hole, avoid driving through the left side or cutting too much corner. Aim for the 150-yard stake for the best approach angle.","Favor left-center off the tee. Carry the approach all the way to the green; there are no run-up shots.","Long hitters can reach in two. Left fairway is shorter but narrower; stay right of center off the tee and favor center or left of the deep green to avoid the sharp right drop-off.","Aim center if the flag is right; wherever the pin is, stay below the hole to avoid a fast downhill putt.","This par 4 plays deceptively long. Stay right of the 150-yard stake off the tee and add a club on approach.","Two fairway sections are separated by a steep drop-off. Long hitters should lay back for a flat lie, then play a high, soft approach to the small green.","Take enough club to carry the tee shot to the center. Long is safer than short, where a deep bunker and steep slope await.","Keep the tee shot left of center on this dogleg right. For a back-right pin, favor left-center of the green to avoid bunker right and trouble behind.","A long par 5 rarely reached in two. Aim at the clubhouse chimney off the tee; lay up right of the 150-yard stake to avoid steep drop-offs left and short of the green."]};
