const backyardGuide={name:'The Back Yard',white:[105,82,72,132,125,88,102,92,113],par:Array(9).fill(3),titles:["Outset","Split-Level","False Front","Goodwill","Tribute","Upper Deck","The Wall","Hideaway","Pressure"],advice:["A gentle uphill shot to a rolling green angled from front-left to back-right. The back-right bunker protects the hole location and prevents right misses from rolling farther downhill.","The only tee set horizontally allows a choice of approach angle to a dramatic two-tiered green. Find the correct tier for a birdie chance; putting between tiers is difficult.","The shortest hole still demands a full carry up to a dramatic false-front green. Short shots roll back off the surface, while shots reaching the green offer a birdie chance.","A classic punchbowl green gives something back to the golfer: the contours gather slightly offline shots toward the putting surface.","A gentler Redan-style green runs diagonally away from right to left, sloping from front-right to back-left. The front-left bunker helps contain left misses.","A pronounced two-tiered green rewards hitting the correct level. Stopping on the wrong tier makes two-putting difficult.","An unusual green offers challenging pin positions, with a revetted grass wall above the front bunker. Two tee boxes provide different angles.","Much of the green is hidden behind mounding near the sixth tee. The large putting surface runs away toward a tucked pin position.","The front thumbprint can yield aces, but other pin locations are demanding. The ninth green is overlooked by the firepit, adding an audience to the final putt."]};
